    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.66,
      "end_seconds": 162.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "I've had high cholesterol, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.37,
      "end_seconds": 171.85,
      "duration_seconds": 8.48,
      "text": "Okay, I can see high cholesterol in your file as well. Do you take any prescribed or over-the-counter medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 173.26,
      "end_seconds": 176.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "It's rosuvastatin, 10 milligrams, at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.47,
      "end_seconds": 181.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "Have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 182.43,
      "end_seconds": 187.05,
      "duration_seconds": 4.62,
      "text": "no, uh, I've never reacted to anything"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.08,
      "end_seconds": 192.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "right, let's have a proper look at you"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.08,
      "end_seconds": 197.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "stay as you are for a moment"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.06,
      "end_seconds": 212.23,
      "duration_seconds": 7.17,
      "text": "The memory test score is a little low today and the rest of the neurological check is normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.5,
      "end_seconds": 217.26,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "You can relax now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.11,
      "end_seconds": 235.67,
      "duration_seconds": 7.56,
      "text": "Taking everything into account, this looks most like a gradual memory problem that needs further assessment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 236.27,
      "end_seconds": 239.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "Do you think it's something serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.14,
      "end_seconds": 250.92,
      "duration_seconds": 9.78,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now a gradual memory problem that needs further assessment is my leading thought, not anything worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.29,
      "end_seconds": 264.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "Let's get a brain scan, for memory loss."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 266.34,
      "end_seconds": 271.28,
      "duration_seconds": 4.94,
      "text": "We have a slot Tuesday at 11:30 am, if that works."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.16,
      "end_seconds": 300.65,
      "duration_seconds": 27.49,
      "text": "Let's get a memory test, for memory loss. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step. Keep a daily routine and write things down, a notebook by the door works well. Keep an eye out, and if you become suddenly confused, call us the same day or go to emergency. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 302.48,
      "end_seconds": 306.58,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "Oh, no, that's all. Thanks a lot."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.05,
      "end_seconds": 309.25,
